cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fBlockKit -- the f-block calculation toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A zero-barrier workbench for strongly correlated systems and lanthanide/actinide
  calculations: it generates calculation input files (basis set, ECP, active space,
  convergence settings) and reads output files or input structures for
  characterisation analysis. It never runs a calculation for the user, does not use
  the network, and does not use machine learning in its decision layer; every
  conclusion carries its provenance (a program-manual quote, a literature DOI, or a
  measured record).
type: software
